TITLE:: PltSpectrum
summary:: Magnitude spectrum, linear or logarithmic in frequency
categories:: Libraries>PlotLib
related:: Overviews/PlotLib, Classes/PltMeter, Classes/FFT, Classes/FreqScope

DESCRIPTION::
Magnitude against frequency, linear by default so partials stay countable, and
logarithmic when the whole range matters.

An link::Classes/FFT:: writes frames into a buffer on the server and the language
polls that buffer. A poll can land in the middle of a frame, which shows as a moment
of noise and is not worth locking against for a picture.

Each pixel column takes the loudest bin that falls in it, so a narrow peak survives
however many bins share a column.

The analysis is rebuilt through link::Classes/ServerTree::, so it comes back after
cmd-period and after a reboot; cmd-period would otherwise take the synth and the
poller's clock with it and leave the last frame frozen on screen.

Compared with link::Classes/FreqScope::: that one draws on the server and is the
cheaper choice for a constantly open analyser. This one keeps the magnitudes in the
language, where strong::mags:: can be read, tested, and drawn on any scale.

note::
FFT output is not normalised: a full scale sine under a Hann window peaks at about
code::fftSize/4::. strong::pushFrame:: scales by the reciprocal, which puts 0 dBFS
at 0 dB on the plot. Verified against tones on exact bin centres in
code::tests/test-live.scd::.
::

CLASSMETHODS::

METHOD:: new
argument:: bus
Bus index to analyse, one channel.
argument:: fftSize
Frame size. Larger resolves frequency more finely and time more coarsely.
argument:: server
argument:: title
argument:: width
argument:: height

METHOD:: magnitudes
Magnitudes from the raw contents of an FFT buffer. scsynth packs a frame as
code::[DC, nyquist, re1, im1, re2, im2, ...]::, so the two purely real bins come
first and are not a complex pair.
returns:: code::fftSize/2 + 1:: magnitudes, bin 0 to nyquist.

METHOD:: binFreq
Centre frequency of a bin.
argument:: bin
argument:: fftSize
argument:: sampleRate

INSTANCEMETHODS::

METHOD:: start
Allocate the buffer, start the analysis synth and the poller.

METHOD:: stop
Free them. strong::close:: does this too.

METHOD:: pushFrame
One frame of magnitudes: scaled, smoothed in time, and folded into the peak hold.

METHOD:: mags
The current magnitudes, bin 0 to nyquist.

METHOD:: logFreq
Logarithmic frequency axis. The labels and the grid move to the frequencies a
listener thinks in.
METHOD:: minHz
Left edge in log mode.
METHOD:: maxHz
Right edge.
METHOD:: floorDb
METHOD:: ceilDb
Top of the scale. Raise it to leave headroom above 0 dBFS.
METHOD:: smooth
Time smoothing, 0 for none.
METHOD:: showHold
METHOD:: holdDecayDb
dB per second the hold trace falls.
METHOD:: pollRate
Frames per second read from the server.
METHOD:: traceColor
METHOD:: holdColor
METHOD:: sampleRate
METHOD:: fftSize
METHOD:: bus
METHOD:: server

EXAMPLES::
code::
s.boot;
x = PltSpectrum(0).front;
y = { Blip.ar(120, 24, 0.3) ! 2 }.play;

x.maxHz_(4000);                  // fill the panel at this pitch
x.logFreq_(true);                // the whole range instead
x.smooth_(0.85);                 // slower, steadier
y.free; x.close;

// a longer frame, for low frequency detail
x = PltSpectrum(0, 4096).logFreq_(true).front;

// which bin is which
PltSpectrum.binFreq(100, 1024, 48000);    // 4687.5
::
